Z||000004||Formula88||07-21-2001||01:52 PM||||I had a similar experience in my 69 Firebird.  Going down the Beltline in Raleigh, I'm coming up on traffic way too fast, when I realize THEY'RE STOPPED!  So I jam the pedal, and burst a wheel cylinder.  Car's still slowing down, but no where near fast enough.  Luckily I still had control, and pulled into the median and went past 2 cars before I came to a stop.  If that wasn't bad enough, after I stopped, a Toyota pickup went sliding past me - he was having a harder time stopping than I was!  Not fun.||||reg||6
