Z||000010||AusFiero||07-22-2001||05:56 AM||||I had a Bug once with a Porsche engine in it and my right running board decided to detach itself at the front mount and crumple under the back wheel at high speed. 360ed it a couple of times on a narrow stretch of highway frequented by mainly trucks. Man it was scarey. Now I remember why I hate VWs.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.auto-alley.com" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A>||202.139.20.3||reg||1
Z||000011||87GTBro||07-24-2001||01:55 PM||||I had a similar experience in my GT that I consider to be nothing short of a miracle.  I was driving to school one rainy morning.  It was one of those freak thunderstorms and it was pouring hard.<P>On the highway it is difficult to see things because of the overspray from the tires of the vehicles in front of you.<P>I was doing about 60, far enough away from the car in front of me so that I could barely see his dim tail lights.<P>All of a sudden, the hazy mist turned to a bright glowing red and the sea of cars traveling in front of me started parting in the middle and all the cars were swerving off onto either side of the highway.<P>I slammed on my brakes and then remembered that the pavement was wet so I backed off a little so the rubber would grip.  I wasn't slowing down fast enough.  I turned the steering wheel to the left and (amazingly) had no understeer.  Usually when you press on the brakes and turn the steering wheel at the same time, the car will keep going straight even though the wheels are turned.  Especially on wet pavement.<P>But I went off the road into the center median still doing about 40 MPH when I hit the grass.  I was sure I was going to hit someone.  I squeezed between another car and a light pole and came to a stop faster than if I was still on the pavement.<P>Then I looked in my rear view mirror to see all these other cars swerving off behind me, so I decided to keep driving in the grass a little further to keep from being rear ended.<P>Then, in the lightning, I saw what caused all the chaos.  This car had rear-ended a truck in the middle of the freeway.  (Don't ask me  how that happened)  The truck was probably going too slow.<P>But I made it with not even a scratch on my baby.  Had a little grass in the wheels and stuck in the e-brake cable, but that's about it.||||reg||1
